  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x200B;&#x200B;Provision of Emergency Shelter and Non-Food Items (NFIs) for Populations Affected by drought and the Northern Ethiopian Crisis&#x200B;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This IOM project provides dignified living conditions and access to essential household items for Internally Displaced Persons and returnees. IOM and its partners provide in-kind emergency shelter and NFI kits, Shelter repair assistance Cash for local material and labor, cash AND Non-Food Items, and technical training on shelter repair assistance and construction. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 46,975 people, including 9,925 women, 10,890 men, 26,160 children, and including 2,932 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
